  "real_edge": "A -> B is a real call when code that the static graph attributes to A (A's own body, or a function/lambda nested in A that has no node of its own) starts executing the body of B, either directly or through code outside the repo (built-ins such as Array.prototype.map/sort, node_modules such as React), inside the same synchronous stack or in A's own continuation after an await/yield. A constructor body counts as the class node (as the static graph names `new C()`); a lambda nested in a variable/class/file node X (a registry entry such as `const actionX = register({ perform: () => ... })`) counts as X.",
  "not_real": "storing, registering or passing a function without running it; a call made by another repo function that received the callback (that function is the caller); code nested in some other node (that node is the caller); a callback run later from the event loop (timer, I/O) is a root, not a call from whoever scheduled it.",
  "dynamic": "kind=dynamic: the call goes through a value (callback parameter, array-method callback, registry/object lookup, stored event callback, option hook). Whether the static graph misses it is computed by the bench (TsIndexer calls edges), not assumed here.",
  "exercised": "exercised=true: the edge runs at least once while vitest runs the repo's listed test files (hand trace from the test to the call site, evidence column).",
  "recovery": "M20 recovery = recorded / (key edges with kind=dynamic, exercised=true, and no static calls edge from->to). Target >= 80%.",
  "invented": "an invented edge is a recorded calls edge that (a) equals a nonEdges pair of the same repo, or (b) names a from/to id that is not a node of that repo's static graph (an id the recorder made up). Target 0. Every recorded edge that touches a key symbol and is neither a key edge nor a static calls edge is listed in the bench details as unverified, for a hand check against the source (procedure in tasks/T28-runtime-flows-from-tests/4 log/key.md); it is reported, and counted as invented if the hand check finds it is not a real call.",
  "overhead": "wall time of `vitest run <the repo test files>` instrumented / plain, median of 3 runs each, measured per repo; target <= 2.0x for each."
